<section id="part-a-3-3"><h3>3.3 Visual anagrams</h3>
<p>At each step, I predicted one guided velocity in the upright view and another in the view rotated 180°. I rotated the second velocity back and averaged the two before the Euler update. The supplied rotation helper flips both spatial axes and passed the supplied identity check when applied twice. I used the skeleton’s prompt pairs. These runs use seeds 180 and 181, h = 0.02, and w = 7.</p>
